-- title:
--   Unique place above P in a constant field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K, F, K', F'$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $F'$ a $K'$-algebra, together with algebra maps $K \to K'$, $F \to F'$ and $K \to F'$ compatible as scalar towers $K \to K' \to F'$ and $K \to F \to F'$, and let $K$ be algebraically closed. Assume $F$ is a function field in one variable over $K$, in the sense that some $x \in F$ is transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over $K(x)$, and likewise that some $x' \in F'$ is transcendental over $K'$ with $F'$ finite-dimensional over $K'(x')$. Assume moreover `IsCurveOver K F`: every nonzero $f \in F$ admits a divisor $D$ of degree $0$ with $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v(f)$ at every place $v$, every place of $F/K$ has residue field finite over $K$, and $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$. Assume finally that $F'$ is generated over $K'$ by the image of $F$, i.e. the subfield of $F'$ generated by $K'$ and $\operatorname{range}(F \to F')$ is all of $F'$. Here a place of $F$ over $K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, and a principal ideal ring, and $\operatorname{ord}$ denotes minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation. Then for every place $P$ of $F$ over $K$ there is a place $P'$ of $F'$ over $K'$ whose valuation subring contracts along $F \to F'$ to that of $P$, which satisfies $\operatorname{ord}_{P'}(f) = \operatorname{ord}_P(f)$ for all $f \in F$, and which is the unique place of $F'$ over $K'$ contracting to $P$.
--
--   This is the classical statement that in a constant field extension of a function field over an algebraically closed constant field, every place has exactly one extension and that extension is unramified; the hypothesis that $K$ be algebraically closed replaces a characteristic-zero assumption, the separating element needed for a primitive element being available because $K$ is perfect. It underlies the conorm map on divisors and degree-zero divisor class groups under constant field extension, and the comparison of Riemann–Roch data and canonical divisors before and after such an extension.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_exists_comap_algebraMap_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed.lean

import Mathlib
